fujinet-go-atari7800-desktop -- milestone log
=============================================

The plan is the family's (see fujinet-go-adam-desktop/PORTING.md): one C API
in core/, four native frontends, FujiNet in-process, one shared settings
store, a native debugger everywhere, no panels visible at startup,
clone-and-build CI. Nothing below is marked done on "it compiles".

M0  scaffold                                                          [x]
  [x] carried from fujinet-go-nes-desktop (core, frontends, CI, packaging)
      and fujinet-go-sms-desktop (BIOS import, roms.c, embed-roms.py)
  [x] identity: online.fujinet.go.atari7800.*, BoIP 11510 / web UI 11511,
      accent and icon background #F0932F (the 2600's mark, inverted)
  [x] cmake/Dependencies.cmake: MAME as the fork's pinned source archive
      (SHA-256 checked), fujinet-firmware c68e8630; MAME_SRC / FUJINET_SRC
  [x] tools/fujinet patch 0002: .a78 is a ROM image CONFIG can push

M1  the FujiNet cartridge in MAME (tschak909/mame fujinet-go-a7800)   [x]
  [x] graft from fujinet-firmware add-atari7800 03b925719 (apply.sh), with
      FUJINET_SOURCES (per-file SHA-256) and fujinet_sync.sh
  [x] mailbox service on a worker thread (the cart's core0), publish
      shadow with ACKSEQ last, loads behind a mutex, sync before SWAP
  [x] fujilink: POSIX + Winsock, non-blocking, redials
  [x] "none" BIOS for a7800 and a7800p; no-BIOS forces DIRECT hand-over
  [x] staged / direct boots of a host image; the High Score Cart

M2  libmame_fngo                                                      [x]
  [x] STANDALONE target fngo (a7800, a7800p only), headless OSD keeping a
      render target live, frames via the screen bitmap + adjusted palette,
      48 kHz stereo, throttle off (the host paces)
  [x] fngo_mame.h C API: lifecycle, input, the FujiNet cart, images/plans,
      the debugger engine (registers, disassembly, breakpoints,
      watchpoints, console, views), state; exports only fngo_mame_*
      (version script / export list / dllexport); mame_exports test
  [x] builds with MAME's own make from CMake (cmake/BuildMame.cmake);
      MinGW cross build of mame_fngo.dll

M3  core                                                              [x]
  [x] MameHost: emulation thread, vsync phase lock / wall-clock pacing,
      adaptive audio resampler, input diffing onto ioports, jobs on the
      emulation thread, cartridge watch for AUTO controllers
  [x] session: no-BIOS boot, staged Open Cartridge, power cycle, Reboot to
      CONFIG, region from header / DB, BIOS per console with fallback to
      none, HSC, console switches, difficulty persistence, light-gun pointer
  [x] media: .a78/.bin/.zip/.7z, BIOS/HSC recognised by CRC whatever the
      name, SD import unpacks
  [x] tests: session, bindings, media, gamepad, debug, fujibus_smoke,
      netboot (A7800_TESTROM_DIR), headless_{config,staged,direct,pal},
      mame_exports, no_embedded_roms_*

M4  debugger                                                          [x]
  [x] a7800debug over MAME's engine: attach/stop/step/over/out/frame/run
      to, MARIA, I/O, cartridge, breakpoints + watchpoints, symbols,
      refused commands (state save/load, hardreset, exit)

M5  ROM sweep (tools/romsweep)                                        [x]
  [x] 114 games of a 116-file No-Intro set: no BIOS, BIOS staged/direct,
      network boot all pass; BIOS boot == stock MAME pixel for pixel
      (5 titles stock MAME itself garbles, checked by hand); BIOS-less and
      network boots line up with the BIOS boot (attract-mode divergences
      checked by hand). REPORT.md committed.

M6  light gun                                                         [x]
  [x] XG-1 in a7800.cpp: CONTROLLERS per port, trigger on Up, sensor on
      INPT4/5, the TIA-cycle penalty with a gun attached
  [x] calibrated against Barnyard Blaster's bullet holes and Meltdown's
      buttons, NTSC and PAL; the five gun titles auto-detected by CRC
  [ ] played by hand with a mouse in each frontend

M7  GNOME + KDE                                                       [x]
  [x] menus, Preferences, Controllers (two ProLine pads, console switches,
      Map), debugger (7 tabs), light-gun crosshair + pointer, drag & drop,
      status line; A7800_SCREENSHOT hook; desktop/metainfo validated
  [x] smoke-run headless (Broadway, Qt offscreen), every window captured
  [ ] hand checklist on a real desktop (input, Map, drag & drop, dialogs)

M8  Windows + macOS                                                   [x]
  [x] Win32 port; cross-builds with mame_fngo.dll; imports system-only
  [x] AppKit port (A7800* classes), libmame_fngo.dylib in Frameworks
  [x] native MSYS2 build and tests in CI (fujibus_smoke against a native
      FujiNet included); macOS arm64 + x86_64 build and tests in CI
  [ ] a look on real Windows and macOS desktops

M9  packaging and release                                             [x]
  [x] Flatpaks with a mame-fngo module; CPack DEB/RPM/TGZ carrying
      libmame_fngo; NSIS + portable zip with mame_fngo.dll; macOS zips
      for both architectures, Frameworks signed
  [x] CI caches MAME's source and objects per pin
  [x] CI green everywhere; v0.1.0 tagged -> draft release with all 12
      assets (DEB/RPM/TGZ x2, two Flatpaks, NSIS + zip, macOS x2)
  [ ] publish the draft after the hand checks above

Later
  [ ] paddles (no 7800 title needs them)
  [ ] MAME's own cart boards as a fallback for images the FujiNet cart
      refuses (XM, XBoard, Versaboard, Megacart)
  [ ] drop patch 0002 once the firmware pin carries .a78 as a ROM type
